      "note": "Allen & Heath Avantis technical datasheet (dealer-hosted copy), opened 2026-11-12: 917 x 627 x 269 mm (W x D x H), 26 kg, 24 motorised faders, two 15.6 in screens; rear: 12 mic/line XLR inputs, 12 XLR line outputs, AES3 input (1) and outputs (2) on XLR, word clock BNC in/out, SLink (proprietary, not modelled), two I/O option card slots (not modelled), two RJ45 network ports, USB (type not named, not modelled); front: 1/4 in and 1/8 in headphone sockets (under the armrest); internal mains supply on an IEC inlet (type letter not named: iec-c14 assumed, plan assumedConnectors power-in); a mains switch near the inlet (datasheet \"Two Pole Push-Button\", guide \"rocker\"). Modelled: 8 of 12 mic inputs and 8 of 12 line outputs. No master fader or other control is documented, so the only control is power. The Getting Started Guide (CCI-hosted) adds a USB 3.0 on the front panel. Generic artwork only (content/generic-panels/<id>.json, drawn by npm run asset:panel): connectors, faders, knobs and screens drawn without lettering, no photo, no logo. Every port and control position is a guess (confidence guess) and the side profile is an estimate drawn from the three outer sizes (no drawing opened). Connector genders not stated by the source follow the convention input = female, output = male."
    },
